# Owners: who holds which work under the charter (charter.md), and until when.
#
# One entry per piece of work, keyed by work.  A claim is its owner, its pending item, and its
# until.  An entry with no owner line is free.
#
#   o list '[*]' docs/working/owners.tony -trim '{work, owner}'   # who owns what
#   o get '(deployment).owner' docs/working/owners.tony           # who holds one
#
# Claiming is an announcement: add an entry and push.  A claim names a pending item and an
# until, the deadline for engaging that item.  The default is one month, and the charter caps
# it at three.  An owner is told before until arrives, and renews by engaging with the item or
# by naming a new deadline.  When until passes the ownership is void, and any charter owner
# may claim the work.  Keep overlap between claims small.
#
# A claim over a working note NAMES THE NOTE: work: task-budget claims work/task-budget.md, so
# the join needs no table.  `make claims` reads this file, the notes and the residual issues and
# says who holds what, what has lapsed and what is free.
#
# A commit under a claim names it in a Work: trailer, so the log shows when the claim was last
# engaged with (contributing.md).  A note may carry one `Claimed: <owner> until <date>` line,
# which `make check` holds to what is written here; a note that says nothing is free to be free.
#
# until is a quoted string because tony reads a bare 2026-10-19 as a malformed number.

!key(work)
- work:  charter
  owner: walter@example.com
  item:  "adoption"
  until: "2026-10-19"

- work:  deployment
  owner: walter@example.com
  item:  "a shared instance runs a deploy/<I>.N tag, annotated with its components"
  until: "2026-10-19"

- work:  gates-reach-users
  item:  "a gate reaches its answerers in slack, and is answered there"

- work:  tracking-unclaimed
  item:  "what is in work and what is free, derived here rather than kept by hand"

- work:  vocabulary-measurement-review
  item:  "read the submission and say what the team does about it"

- work: permissions-review
  item: "review permissions in ENG-1256"
